Pin the mcp dependency below 2.0 so the built-in MCP servers import.

Upstream https://github.com/odysseus-dev/odysseus/issues/6165 and #6209
(both open for main). Fixed on dev in 01790c2f0 ("fix(mcp): keep
built-in servers on SDK v1"), never merged to main, which `src` pins.

Unpinned, pip resolves mcp 2.x, whose SDK drops @server.list_tools();
all four built-in MCP servers (Email, Memory, RAG, Image Generation)
then crash at startup and the agent gets none of their tools.

--- a/requirements.txt
+++ b/requirements.txt
@@ -38,7 +38,9 @@
 caldav
 cryptography
 bcrypt
-mcp
+# The built-in MCP servers use the v1 SDK's @server.list_tools(); mcp 2.x
+# removed it. Upstream dev pins this too (01790c2f0); main does not yet.
+mcp<2
 pyotp
 qrcode[pil]
 croniter
